description:
Add two new events to OctoPi.Agent.Event for the compaction lifecycle.
These are emitted by the manual compaction API and the auto-compaction path in the Loop.

Reference: tmp/pi-mono/packages/coding-agent/src/core/agent-session.ts lines 121-129.

## Add to apps/octo_pi_agent/lib/octo_pi/agent/event.ex

defmodule CompactionStart do
  @moduledoc "Emitted when context compaction begins."
  @enforce_keys [:reason]
  @type reason :: :manual | :threshold | :overflow
  @type t :: %__MODULE__{reason: reason()}
  defstruct [:reason]
end

defmodule CompactionEnd do
  @moduledoc "Emitted when compaction finishes, is cancelled, or fails."
  @enforce_keys [:reason, :aborted?, :will_retry?]
  @type reason :: :manual | :threshold | :overflow
  @type t :: %__MODULE__{
    reason: reason(),
    result: map() | nil,
    aborted?: boolean(),
    will_retry?: boolean(),
    error_message: String.t() | nil
  }
  defstruct [:reason, :result, :error_message, aborted?: false, will_retry?: false]
end

result is %{summary: String.t(), first_kept_entry_id: String.t(), tokens_before: integer()}
when compaction succeeded, nil when aborted or failed.

will_retry?: true means overflow triggered compaction and the agent will
automatically retry the failed turn after compaction completes.

## Also update the @type t :: union in event.ex

Add Event.CompactionStart.t() | Event.CompactionEnd.t() to the union.

## Tests

Add to the event test file (create one if it doesn't exist).
Verify struct shapes; verify the union type includes the new variants.
